From 9466697f6491396c17fcdccb392674d7759e7a96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mabn <github@mabn.pl>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:22:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 151/156] [barreplay] H124 + P12 v3: calls that change no
 vector or collision input skip P8's drain and P12's mark (toggle3 0x80000 /
 0x100000)

speed62's profile: P8's make-every-unit-ready (EnsureAllSlow) is 0.75% of the
main thread, and luaprof63 puts the largest share under BAR's stockpile gadget,
whose StockpileChanged callin (in the weapon loop) gives stockpile orders.
speed58's whole-game tally of the loop's draining calls: SpawnCEG 33,798,
GiveOrderToUnit 13,719, GetUnitWeaponState 6,996, GetUnitWeaponVectors 1,303.

BrNoSimInput: GetUnitWeaponState and GetUnitWeaponVectors are reads (in the
draining list for P4; the second ensures its own unit), SpawnCEG spawns only
unsynced effects, and a stockpile order on a unit whose stockpile command is
non-queueing reaches ExecuteStateCommand through every command AI without a
queueing command's side effects, changing the stockpile queue and the icon.
Lua callins on the way come through the trampoline themselves.

Also: after a frame's first EnsureAll every unit is ready (a state only goes
0 -> 1 -> 2 until the next Begin), so the next ones visit nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
